# Trusted signers of lovverk publication seals (docs/publication-seal.md).
# OpenSSH allowed_signers format (ssh-keygen(1), "ALLOWED SIGNERS"); lines
# starting with "#" and blank lines are ignored.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE: no seal key has been installed yet. While this file holds
# no key line, `lovspor publication-seal verify` refuses every seal, so the
# sync job fails before any push whenever it has produced a seal.
#
# One line per key, namespace "git" (git's SSH signing namespace), optionally
# bounded in time for a rotation overlap (UTC, checked against the tagger date):
#
#   lovverk-publication-seal namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 <key>
#   lovverk-publication-seal namespaces="git",valid-before="YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ" ssh-ed25519 <old key>
#   lovverk-publication-seal namespaces="git",valid-after="YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ" ssh-ed25519 <new key>
#
# Public keys only. A change here is an owner-reviewed, owner-merged change.
